{
  "reason": "Pin the current Discord access file and renderer shapes, delivery normalization, and engine-owned permission projection. Expired pairing codes are rejected before granting access, and sender IDs cannot become paths outside the approved drop-box. Permission prefixes follow the engine-owned literal grammar; backslashes are never decoded as UI escaping, so existing UNC and shell commands keep their meaning.",
  "emptyAccess": {
    "dmPolicy": "pairing",
